From 20891a25818d464e8bab614258454dcc8819e590 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: flashnext <flashnext@leger.run>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 23:09:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] [ROCm] Enable block-FP8 fused MoE on gfx1151 via
 in-kernel upcast

gfx1151 (Strix Halo, RDNA3.5) is recognised throughout platforms/rocm.py
(_ON_GFX1151 at :220, the Radeon 8060S PCI id at :78) but is excluded from
supports_fp8() at :971-972, which returns `on_cdna() or on_rdna4()`. That
single predicate is what TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme keys on, so a
128x128 block-FP8 MoE checkpoint dispatches to no kernel class at all: every
one of the 14 backends in oracle/fp8.py:_AVAILABLE_BACKENDS rejects, and
select_fp8_moe_backend raises

    NotImplementedError: No FP8 MoE backend supports the deployment
    configuration.

from oracle/fp8.py:413-416, during layer construction, before a single
expert weight byte is read.

The exclusion is a statement about the *matrix unit*: RDNA3.5 has no FP8
WMMA, so tl.dot cannot consume fp8 operands. It is not a statement about
whether the Triton fused MoE kernel can serve the scheme -- it can, by
converting the loaded tiles to bf16 immediately before tl.dot, exactly the
mechanism upstream added for the block-scaled *linear* kernel in
vllm-project/vllm#52970 (FORCE_FP8_DOT_UPCAST in fp8_utils.py).

This does the same for the MoE path:

* fused_moe/utils.py gains the FN_FP8_MOE latch (read once at import,
  default on) plus fp8_moe_gfx1151_admitted() and
  fp8_moe_gfx1151_dot_upcast(). The latter additionally requires
  Triton < 3.8.0, matching #52970 -- newer Triton lowers an fp8 tl.dot on
  gfx1151 itself.

* TritonExperts._supports_quant_scheme appends only
  (kFp8Static128BlockSym, kFp8Dynamic128Sym) when admitted, and logs once
  at admission. The per-tensor/per-channel schemes take the fp8_fast_accum
  `tl.dot(a, b, acc=accumulator)` path, which the upcast does not cover, so
  they stay refused.

* fused_moe_kernel gains a FORCE_FP8_DOT_UPCAST tl.constexpr (default
  False) that converts the A/B tiles to bf16 after the K-loop loads.
  invoke_fused_moe_triton_kernel is the sole launch site of that kernel in
  the tree, so this covers the gate/up projection, the down projection and
  the non-modular fused_experts_impl chunked path in one place. It logs
  once when engaged.

FN_FP8_MOE=0 disables admission and upcast together, restoring the stock
refusal byte-for-byte. Nothing outside the MoE oracle changes:
RocmPlatform.supports_fp8() is deliberately untouched.

Adds tests/kernels/moe/test_gfx1151_fp8_admission.py, a GPU-free
monkeypatched pin on the admission, the kill switch, the gfx1151-only scope
and the Triton version gate.
